# --- the realm ----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One king, his queen, and every house sworn to him. `wants an heir` is the
# edge the naming of an heir consumes; a king's death inserts `wants a king`,
# which the heir takes by an always-rule and a pretender by a chance - they
# compete for the same edge, so the claim pass decides between them.

Aldric_Aldring is king of Wessex
Maerwyn_Aldring is queen of Wessex
Wessex wants an heir

# The king's own house swears to nobody: `the-kings-house-swears-to-no-one`
# would take the oath back anyway, and while it stood the king could be found
# declaring for a pretender against himself.
Wulfing swears to Wessex
Godring swears to Wessex
Ceolring swears to Wessex
